  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "When the sum of the first ten terms of an arithmetic progression is four times the sum of the first five terms, the ratio of the first term to the common difference is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1:2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2:1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1:4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(4:1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(1:1\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "1:2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1952-p30.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sum formula gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} S_{10}&=5(2a+9d),\\\\ S_5&=\\frac52(2a+4d). \\end{aligned} \\] The equation \\(S_{10}=4S_5\\) becomes \\[ 2a+9d=2(2a+4d), \\] so \\(d=2a.\\) Hence \\(a:d=1:2.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write both partial sums in terms of the first term \\(a\\) and common difference \\(d\\)",
        "Use \\(S_n=\\dfrac n2(2a+(n-1)d)\\) and simplify \\(S_{10}=4S_5\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
